==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|prognostick}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|prognosticus}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|προγνωστικός||foreknowing}}, from {{m|grc|πρό-}} + {{m|grc|γνωστικός||of or for knowing, good at knowing}}, from {{m|grc|γιγνώσκω||to learn to know, to perceive, to mark, to learn}}.
Compare {{cog|fr|pronostic||prognostic}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, pertaining to or characterized by [[prognosis]] or [[prediction]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|foretelling}}
* {{l|en|predictive}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|of or pertaining to prognosis}}
* Finnish: {{t|fi|ennusteellinen}}
* French: {{t+|fr|pronostique}}
* Italian: {{t+|it|prognostico}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Portuguese: {{t+|pt|prognóstico}}
